IMPORT prelude

-- Health Insurance Act 1973 (Cth) -- what Medicare means for the patient: am I an "eligible person" (s 3(1) "Australian
-- resident", "eligible overseas representative"; ss 6, 6A, 7); is a Medicare benefit payable for my service (s 10(1), (1A);
-- s 17(1)(a); s 19(1)-(6)); how much is it (ss 9, 10(2)-(5), 14(1), with the services the Regulations prescribe for 100%);
-- who is paid, what bulk billing is and what I can then be charged (ss 20(1), (2), 20A(1)); the Medicare safety nets as far
-- as the Act states them (ss 8(1A), 10AC, 10ACA, 10AD, 10ADA); and whether I can be charged as a public patient in a public
-- hospital (s 3(1) "public hospital service", "public patient", "recognised hospital"; s 128C).
--
-- SEAT: the patient (the Medicare-eligible person) -- "Am I covered by Medicare, and what will I pay?". Every exported
-- question is the patient's: "Am I an eligible person?", "Is a Medicare benefit payable for my service?", "How much Medicare
-- benefit do I get?", "How much will I be out of pocket?", "Is my bulk-billing agreement valid?", "Does this claim take me
-- over the Medicare safety net?", "Does s 128C forbid the doctor charging me as a public patient?". Where the Act hands a
-- judgment to someone else (a Ministerial order or direction, s 6, s 19; the Chief Executive Medicare being satisfied,
-- ss 10AC-10ADA), it is asked as a fact the patient can state.
--
-- Provisions covered: s 3(1) (the definitions above, "eligible person", "professional service" as a fact); ss 6(1), (2),
-- 6A(1), 7(2) (their effect, as facts); s 8(1A) ("concessional person", "FTB(A) family", "patient contribution", the four
-- safety-net amounts, "Schedule fee"); s 9; s 10(1)-(5); s 10AC(1), (2); s 10ACA(1)-(5), (7) (the straddling increase as an
-- input); s 10AD(2), (3); s 10ADA(2)-(6), (8) (likewise); s 14(1); s 17(1)(a); s 19(1)-(6); s 20(1), (2); s 20A(1);
-- s 128C(1), (2).
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 136, compilation date 19 September 2026 (includes amendments up to Act No. 90, 2026), register id
-- C2026C00411, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A00101.txt. Regulations: Health Insurance Regulations
-- 2018, Compilation No. 26, compilation date 1 July 2026 (register id F2026C00551), as deposited at
-- ../../../health-insurance-regulations-2018/registers/source-bundle/F2018L01365.txt -- s 28(1) table item 1 (the Group A1
-- items at 100% of the Schedule fee), ss 65B, 65C(6) (what a bulk-billing agreement must be), s 90 (when a public patient
-- must not be charged). NOT DEPOSITED: the Health Insurance (General Medical Services Table) Regulations (the Medicare
-- Benefits Schedule), so every Schedule fee is an INPUT; the regulations under s 6A, which are not in the 2018 Regulations,
-- so being covered by them is an INPUT.
--
-- AMOUNTS ARE INPUTS. The greatest permissible gap ($50.00, s 10(5)) and the four safety-net amounts ($246, $500, $500,
-- $2,000, s 8(1A)) are indexed every year under s 10A. The figures printed in the compilation are therefore not the figures
-- in force in any given year. The safety-net questions take a `Safety-net amounts` record; `the safety-net amounts as
-- printed in Compilation No. 136` holds the printed figures, for use as labelled examples. The $50.00 gap is applied as
-- printed.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: whether a service is a "professional service" (an item relates to it; "clinically relevant") -- a fact;
-- the rows of the s 28 table beyond Group A1, and its diagnostic imaging limb (s 28(2)) -- a fact; the multiple-operation,
-- anaesthesia, pathology, diagnostic imaging and radiation oncology rules (ss 15-16G); s 17(1)(b)-(d); s 19(3)(b)
-- (industrial undertakings); the practitioner-side bars (ss 19AA-19C) and the My Health Record rules (ss 19AD-19AI);
-- s 14(2); the cheque route under s 20(2A)-(6); enduring agreements beyond the fact that reg 65CB is met; simplified billing
-- (s 20A(2), s 20AAA); claims (s 20B); family registration and changes of family (ss 10AA, 10AB, 10AE) beyond the fact of
-- being in a registered family; the s 10B caps on extended safety-net increases (ss 10ACA(7A)-(7B), 10ADA(8A)-(8B)); the
-- formula in ss 10ACA(7) and 10ADA(8), which is missing from the deposit; indexation mechanics (s 10A); and Parts IIA
-- onwards except s 128C. Recovery of Medicare benefits out of compensation or damages (k044) is not in this Act (NOTES.md).
-- The 1996, 2003 and 2006 events of the lives are answered under this 2026 compilation.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the
-- individual to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Health Insurance Act 1973 -- Medicare, from the patient's seat`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `s 3(1) -- am I an eligible person`

-- s 3(1): "Australian resident means a person who resides in Australia and who is: (a) an Australian citizen; or (b) ... the
-- holder of a permanent visa; or (ba) a person who has been granted, or who is included in, a return endorsement or a resident
-- return visa ...; or (c) a New Zealand citizen who is lawfully present in Australia; or (d) a person ... who is lawfully present
-- in Australia and whose continued presence in Australia is not subject to any limitation as to time imposed by law; or (f) a
-- person who: (i) is ... the holder of a temporary visa; and (ia) is not covered by regulations made under subsection 6A(1); and
-- (ii) has applied for a permanent visa ... [still pending]; and (iii) has not, both: (A) ... made an application for a
-- protection visa ... [still pending]; and (B) ... made an application for a parent visa ...; and (iv) has not ... made an
-- application for a parent visa ... [still pending]; and (v) in respect of whom either: (A) another person, being the person's
-- spouse, parent or child ..., is an Australian citizen or the holder of a permanent visa ...; or (B) an authority to work in
-- Australia is in force." (There is no paragraph (e) in the deposit.)
-- "eligible person means an Australian resident or an eligible overseas representative." An "eligible overseas
-- representative" is a head or staff member of a foreign mission or consular post, or a household family member, who is
-- neither a citizen nor domiciled here and is to be treated as a resident under an agreement with that country.
-- There is no age condition and no enrolment condition. The Medicare card and enrolment are not in this Act.
-- s 6(1): the Minister may, by order, declare that a person who "would not be an eligible person" is to be treated as one.
-- s 6(2): by legislative instrument, that a person who "would be an eligible person" is to be treated as not one,
-- "notwithstanding anything in this Act". s 6A(1): regulations may treat a holder of a prescribed temporary visa as an eligible
-- person "while he or she is in Australia". s 7(2): a visitor covered by a reciprocal agreement "shall, subject to the agreement,
-- be treated as an eligible person ... during his or her stay in Australia".
-- Glosses: "resides in Australia" and the visa terms are borrowed (Migration Act 1958) and asked as facts.
DECLARE `Me` HAS
    `I reside in Australia`                                                  IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 3(1) opening words
    `I am an Australian citizen`                                             IS A BOOLEAN  -- (a)
    `I hold a permanent visa`                                                IS A BOOLEAN  -- (b)
    `I have a return endorsement or resident return visa`                    IS A BOOLEAN  -- (ba)
    `I am a New Zealand citizen`                                             IS A BOOLEAN  -- (c)
    `I am lawfully present in Australia`                                     IS A BOOLEAN  -- (c), (d)
    `my stay is not limited in time by law`                                  IS A BOOLEAN  -- (d)
    `I hold a temporary visa`                                                IS A BOOLEAN  -- (f)(i)
    `I am covered by s 6A(1) regulations`                                    IS A BOOLEAN  -- (f)(ia); s 6A
    `my permanent visa application is pending`                               IS A BOOLEAN  -- (f)(ii)
    `I have a pending protection visa application and have applied for a parent visa` IS A BOOLEAN  -- (f)(iii)
    `my parent visa application is pending`                                  IS A BOOLEAN  -- (f)(iv)
    `my spouse, parent or child is a citizen or permanent visa holder`       IS A BOOLEAN  -- (f)(v)(A)
    `I have an authority to work in Australia`                               IS A BOOLEAN  -- (f)(v)(B)
    `I am an eligible overseas representative`                               IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 3(1)
    `a Ministerial order under s 6(1) treats me as eligible`                 IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 6(1)
    `an order under s 6(2) treats me as not eligible`                        IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 6(2)
    `I am a visitor under a reciprocal health care agreement`                IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 7(2)

GIVEN `me` IS A `Me`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I come within paragraph (f)` IF
        `me`'s `I hold a temporary visa`
    AND (NOT (`me`'s `I am covered by s 6A(1) regulations`))
    AND `me`'s `my permanent visa application is pending`
    AND (NOT (`me`'s `I have a pending protection visa application and have applied for a parent visa`))
    AND (NOT (`me`'s `my parent visa application is pending`))
    AND (    `me`'s `my spouse, parent or child is a citizen or permanent visa holder`
         OR  `me`'s `I have an authority to work in Australia`)

@export Am I an Australian resident for Medicare (s 3(1))?
GIVEN `me` IS A `Me` @desc Where you live, your citizenship and your visas
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I an Australian resident` IF
        `me`'s `I reside in Australia`
    AND (    `me`'s `I am an Australian citizen`
         OR  `me`'s `I hold a permanent visa`
         OR  `me`'s `I have a return endorsement or resident return visa`
         OR  (`me`'s `I am a New Zealand citizen` AND `me`'s `I am lawfully present in Australia`)
         OR  (`me`'s `I am lawfully present in Australia` AND `me`'s `my stay is not limited in time by law`)
         OR  `I come within paragraph (f)` `me`)

@export Am I an eligible person for Medicare (s 3(1); ss 6, 6A, 7)?
GIVEN `me` IS A `Me` @desc Where you live, your citizenship and visas, and any order, regulation or agreement that covers you
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I an eligible person` IF
        (    `Am I an Australian resident` `me`
         OR  `me`'s `I am an eligible overseas representative`
         OR  `me`'s `a Ministerial order under s 6(1) treats me as eligible`
         OR  `me`'s `I am covered by s 6A(1) regulations`
         OR  `me`'s `I am a visitor under a reciprocal health care agreement`)
    AND (NOT (`me`'s `an order under s 6(2) treats me as not eligible`))

§§ `ss 10(1), 17, 19 -- is a Medicare benefit payable for my service`

-- s 10(1): "Where, on or after 1 February 1984, medical expenses are incurred in respect of a professional service rendered in
-- Australia to an eligible person, medicare benefit calculated in accordance with subsection (2) is payable". (1A): a service on
-- a "domestic journey" is taken to be rendered in Australia.
-- "medical expenses means an amount payable in respect of a professional service" (s 3(1)). A "professional service" is,
-- broadly, a clinically relevant service by or for a medical practitioner to which an item of the table relates -- asked as a
-- fact.
-- s 17(1): a medicare benefit "is not payable" if "(a) the medical expenses in respect of that service have been paid, or are
-- payable, to a recognized hospital" (paras (b)-(d) are not encoded).
-- s 19(1): not payable for a medical examination for "(a) life insurance; (b) superannuation or provident account schemes; or (c)
-- admission to membership of a friendly society". (2) "Unless the Minister otherwise directs", not payable for a service
-- rendered "by, or on behalf of, or under an arrangement with: (a) the Commonwealth; (b) a State; (c) a local governing body; or
-- (d) an authority established by a law" of the Commonwealth, a State or an internal Territory. (3) "Unless the Minister
-- otherwise directs", not payable if "(a) the medical expenses ... were incurred by the employer". (4) not payable for a service
-- "rendered in the course of the carrying out of a mass immunization". (5) "Unless the Minister otherwise directs", not payable
-- for "a health screening service". (6) not payable unless the prescribed particulars have been recorded on the account or
-- receipt.
-- ENCODING CHOICE: one fact stands for a Ministerial direction disapplying whichever of s 19(2), (3), (5) is engaged.
DECLARE `My service` HAS
    `the patient`                                                            IS A `Me`
    `date rendered as YYYYMMDD`                                              IS A NUMBER   -- s 10(1)
    `rendered in Australia or on a domestic journey`                         IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 10(1), (1A)
    `it is a professional service`                                           IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 3(1)
    `medical expenses are incurred for it`                                   IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 10(1)
    `the expenses are paid or payable to a recognised hospital`              IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 17(1)(a)
    `rendered by or for the Commonwealth, a State, a local body or a statutory authority` IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 19(2)
    `the expenses were incurred by my employer`                              IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 19(3)(a)
    `it is a health screening service`                                       IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 19(5)
    `the Minister has directed otherwise`                                    IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 19(2), (3), (5)
    `it is an examination for life insurance, superannuation or a friendly society` IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 19(1)
    `rendered in a mass immunisation`                                        IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 19(4)
    `the prescribed particulars are on the account`                          IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 19(6)

@export Is a Medicare benefit payable for my service (ss 10(1), 17, 19)?
GIVEN `my service` IS A `My service` @desc The service, when and where it was given, who gave it and who pays for it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a Medicare benefit payable for my service` IF
        `my service`'s `date rendered as YYYYMMDD` AT LEAST 19840201
    AND `my service`'s `rendered in Australia or on a domestic journey`
    AND `Am I an eligible person` (`my service`'s `the patient`)
    AND `my service`'s `it is a professional service`
    AND `my service`'s `medical expenses are incurred for it`
    AND (NOT (`my service`'s `the expenses are paid or payable to a recognised hospital`))
    AND (NOT (`my service`'s `it is an examination for life insurance, superannuation or a friendly society`))
    AND (NOT (`my service`'s `rendered in a mass immunisation`))
    AND (    `my service`'s `the Minister has directed otherwise`
         OR  (    (NOT (`my service`'s `rendered by or for the Commonwealth, a State, a local body or a statutory authority`))
              AND (NOT (`my service`'s `the expenses were incurred by my employer`))
              AND (NOT (`my service`'s `it is a health screening service`))))
    AND `my service`'s `the prescribed particulars are on the account`

§§ `ss 9, 10(2)-(5), 14 -- how much Medicare benefit do I get`

-- s 9: benefits (other than under ss 10ACA and 10ADA) "shall be calculated by reference to the fees for medical services set out
-- in the table". "Schedule fee, in relation to a service, means the fee specified in the table in respect of the service"
-- (s 8(1A)). The table is not deposited: the Schedule fee is an input.
-- s 10(2): "A benefit in respect of a service is: (a) in the case of a service provided: (i) as part of an episode of hospital
-- treatment; or (ii) as part of an episode of hospital-substitute treatment in respect of which the person ... chooses to receive
-- a benefit from a private health insurer; an amount equal to 75% of the Schedule fee; or (aa) in the case of a service to which
-- paragraph (a) does not apply and that is prescribed by the regulations ...--an amount equal to 100% of the Schedule fee; or (b)
-- in any other case--an amount equal to 85% of the Schedule fee."
-- (3): "If the Schedule fee exceeds the amount of benefit calculated under paragraph (2)(b) by more than the greatest permissible
-- gap, the benefit is taken to be the Schedule fee less the greatest permissible gap." (5): "greatest permissible gap means
-- $50.00" (indexed under s 10A; applied here as printed). (4): an amount "not a multiple of 5 cents ... is to be rounded up to
-- the nearest multiple of 5 cents".
-- s 14(1): a benefit "shall not exceed the medical expenses incurred" ((2) is not encoded).
-- ENCODING CHOICE: the rounding in (4) is applied to the (2) amount before the (3) comparison; with Schedule fees that are
-- whole multiples of 5 cents the order makes no difference.
DECLARE `Where my service was given` IS ONE OF
    `outside any episode of hospital treatment`
    `part of an episode of hospital treatment`
    `hospital-substitute treatment with a private insurer benefit chosen`
    `hospital-substitute treatment with no private insurer benefit chosen`

-- Regulations s 28(1): "For the purposes of paragraph 10(2)(aa) of the Act, a service specified in an item of the general
-- medical services table that is listed in the following table is prescribed." Table item 1, Group A1: "3, 4, 23, 24, 36, 37,
-- 44, 47, 123, 124". The other 40-odd rows of the table, and s 28(2) (diagnostic imaging), are asked as one fact.
`the Group A1 items prescribed for 100 per cent by reg 28` MEANS
    LIST 3, 4, 23, 24, 36, 37, 44, 47, 123, 124

@export Is my service prescribed for a benefit of 100% of the Schedule fee (s 10(2)(aa); Regulations s 28)?
GIVEN `the item number` IS A NUMBER @desc The item number of the Medicare Benefits Schedule for your service
      `the item is listed in another row of the reg 28 table` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the item is listed in a row of the Regulations s 28 table other than Group A1 (or is a diagnostic imaging service under s 28(2))
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my service prescribed for 100 per cent` IF
        elem `the item number` `the Group A1 items prescribed for 100 per cent by reg 28`
    OR  `the item is listed in another row of the reg 28 table`

@export What percentage of the Schedule fee is my Medicare benefit (s 10(2))?
GIVEN `where` IS A `Where my service was given` @desc Whether the service was part of hospital or hospital-substitute treatment
      `prescribed for 100 per cent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Regulations prescribe the service for 100% (s 28)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What percentage of the Schedule fee is my benefit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `where`
    WHEN `part of an episode of hospital treatment` THEN 75
    WHEN `hospital-substitute treatment with a private insurer benefit chosen` THEN 75
    OTHERWISE IF `prescribed for 100 per cent` THEN 100 ELSE 85

`the greatest permissible gap` MEANS 50

GIVEN `x` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rounded up to 5 cents` MEANS
    (0 MINUS FLOOR (0 MINUS (`x` TIMES 20))) DIVIDED BY 20

GIVEN `the Schedule fee` IS A NUMBER, `where` IS A `Where my service was given`, `prescribed for 100 per cent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the benefit under s 10` MEANS
    IF      `What percentage of the Schedule fee is my benefit` `where` `prescribed for 100 per cent` EQUALS 85
        AND `the Schedule fee` MINUS `the calculated amount` GREATER THAN `the greatest permissible gap`
    THEN `the Schedule fee` MINUS `the greatest permissible gap`
    ELSE `the calculated amount`
    WHERE
        `the calculated amount` MEANS
            `rounded up to 5 cents`
                (`the Schedule fee` TIMES `What percentage of the Schedule fee is my benefit` `where` `prescribed for 100 per cent` DIVIDED BY 100)

@export How much Medicare benefit do I get for my service, in dollars (ss 10(2)-(5), 14(1))?
GIVEN `the Schedule fee` IS A NUMBER @desc The Schedule fee for the item, in dollars
      `where` IS A `Where my service was given` @desc Whether the service was part of hospital or hospital-substitute treatment
      `prescribed for 100 per cent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Regulations prescribe the service for 100% (s 28)
      `the medical expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc What you were charged for the service, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much Medicare benefit do I get` MEANS
    `the lesser of` (`the benefit under s 10` `the Schedule fee` `where` `prescribed for 100 per cent`)
                    `the medical expenses`

§§ `ss 20(1), (2), 20A(1); Regulations ss 65B, 65C -- bulk billing; who is paid; what I can be charged`

-- s 20(1): the benefit "is payable ... to the person who incurs the medical expenses in respect of that service". (2): where
-- that person "has not paid the medical expenses ... he or she shall not be paid the medicare benefit but, if he or she so
-- requests", is given "a cheque for the amount of the medicare benefit drawn in favour of the person by whom, or on whose behalf,
-- the professional service was rendered".
-- s 20A(1) ("Bulk billing assignments"): an eligible person "may enter into an agreement to assign the assignor's right to the
-- payment of the medicare benefit if: (a) the professional service is or will be rendered to the assignor or to another eligible
-- person; and (b) the agreement is entered into with the person by whom, or on whose behalf, the professional service is or will
-- be rendered (the professional); and (c) the agreement provides that: (i) the assignor assigns ... ; and (ii) the professional
-- accepts the assignment in full payment of the medical expenses ...; and (d) any requirements specified in the regulations are
-- met."
-- Regulations s 65B: "For the purposes of paragraph 20A(1)(d) of the Act, the agreement must be: (a) an episodic agreement that
-- meets the requirements specified in section 65C ...; or (b) an enduring agreement that meets the requirements specified in
-- section 65CB". s 65C(4): the professional "must ensure that the assignor is given the following information, in writing,
-- before or at the time either party offers entry"; (6): "The agreement must: (a) include the information that was required to
-- be given ...; and (b) specify whether the assignor is the person to whom the agreement service is or will be rendered; and (c)
-- be a written agreement that is signed and dated by the assignor." s 65CB (enduring agreements) is asked as one fact.
-- READING (an inference from s 20A(1)(c)(ii)): once a valid bulk-billing agreement is made, the patient owes nothing for the
-- service. Nothing in the Act obliges a professional to offer one.
DECLARE `Kind of agreement` IS ONE OF
    `an episodic agreement`
    `an enduring agreement`

DECLARE `My bulk-billing agreement` HAS
    `I am an eligible person`                                                IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 20A(1)
    `the service is for me or another eligible person`                       IS A BOOLEAN  -- (a)
    `the agreement is with the professional who renders the service`        IS A BOOLEAN  -- (b)
    `I assign my right to the benefit to the professional`                   IS A BOOLEAN  -- (c)(i)
    `the professional accepts it in full payment`                            IS A BOOLEAN  -- (c)(ii)
    `the kind of agreement`                                                  IS A `Kind of agreement`  -- reg 65B
    `I was given the reg 65C(4) information in writing and it is in the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN  -- reg 65C(4), (6)(a)
    `it says whether the service is for me`                                  IS A BOOLEAN  -- reg 65C(6)(b)
    `it is in writing, signed and dated by me`                               IS A BOOLEAN  -- reg 65C(6)(c)
    `it meets the reg 65CB requirements for enduring agreements`             IS A BOOLEAN  -- reg 65CB

GIVEN `the agreement` IS A `My bulk-billing agreement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the regulation requirements are met` IF
    CONSIDER `the agreement`'s `the kind of agreement`
    WHEN `an episodic agreement` THEN
            `the agreement`'s `I was given the reg 65C(4) information in writing and it is in the agreement`
        AND `the agreement`'s `it says whether the service is for me`
        AND `the agreement`'s `it is in writing, signed and dated by me`
    WHEN `an enduring agreement` THEN `the agreement`'s `it meets the reg 65CB requirements for enduring agreements`

@export Is my bulk-billing agreement valid (s 20A(1); Regulations ss 65B, 65C)?
GIVEN `the agreement` IS A `My bulk-billing agreement` @desc The agreement you signed with the doctor or other professional
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my bulk-billing agreement valid` IF
        `the agreement`'s `I am an eligible person`
    AND `the agreement`'s `the service is for me or another eligible person`
    AND `the agreement`'s `the agreement is with the professional who renders the service`
    AND `the agreement`'s `I assign my right to the benefit to the professional`
    AND `the agreement`'s `the professional accepts it in full payment`
    AND `the regulation requirements are met` `the agreement`

@export How much will I be out of pocket for my service, in dollars (ss 10, 20A(1)(c)(ii))?
GIVEN `the fee charged` IS A NUMBER @desc What you are charged for the service, in dollars
      `my Medicare benefit` IS A NUMBER @desc Your Medicare benefit for the service, in dollars
      `bulk billed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you made a valid bulk-billing agreement for the service
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much will I be out of pocket` MEANS
    IF `bulk billed` THEN 0 ELSE `the greater of` 0 (`the fee charged` MINUS `my Medicare benefit`)

DECLARE `Who my benefit is paid to` IS ONE OF
    `the professional, under my bulk-billing assignment`
    `me`
    `nobody unless I ask for a cheque made out to the professional`

@export Who is my Medicare benefit paid to (ss 20(1), (2), 20A(1))?
GIVEN `bulk billed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you made a valid bulk-billing agreement for the service
      `I have paid the bill` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have paid the professional's account
GIVETH A `Who my benefit is paid to`
`Who is my benefit paid to` MEANS
    IF `bulk billed` THEN `the professional, under my bulk-billing assignment`
    ELSE IF `I have paid the bill` THEN `me`
         ELSE `nobody unless I ask for a cheque made out to the professional`

§§ `ss 8(1A), 10AC, 10AD -- the Medicare safety net`

-- s 8(1A): "patient contribution, in relation to a claim for benefit in respect of a service, means an amount equal to the
-- difference between: (a) the Schedule fee or, if the medical expenses in respect of the service are less than that fee, those
-- expenses; and (b) the amount of benefit that, apart from section 10AC, 10ACA, 10AD or 10ADA ..., would be payable". "safety-net
-- amount means $246" (indexed under s 10A).
-- s 10AC(1): "relevant service means a service: (a) in respect of which benefit is payable; and (b) the medical expenses in
-- respect of which exceed the amount of benefit that, apart from this section, would be payable ...; but does not include a
-- service rendered to a person while hospital treatment, or hospital-substitute treatment in respect of which the person chooses
-- to receive a benefit from a private health insurer, is provided to the person".
-- s 10AD(3) (a person not in a registered family; s 10AC(2) is the same for a registered family, counting every member's
-- claims): if the threshold claim is accepted, the prior claims were accepted before it, and the Chief Executive Medicare is
-- satisfied that "(i) the medical expenses ... have been paid; and (ii) the sum of the patient contributions that have been paid
-- in respect of those prior claims is less than the safety-net amount for that year; and (iii) the sum of the patient
-- contribution in respect of the threshold claim and the patient contributions referred to in subparagraph (ii) is equal to or
-- exceeds the safety-net amount", then the benefit for the threshold service and every later service in the year "is increased
-- by the amount of the patient contribution in respect of that service".
-- ENCODING CHOICE: the Chief Executive Medicare's satisfaction is read as the facts it is satisfied of; claims accepted in date
-- order; the s 10AC(2A) and s 10AD(3A) reduction for amounts already paid under the extended safety net is not applied (the
-- prior contributions are taken net of it, as stated by the patient).
DECLARE `Safety-net amounts` HAS
    `the safety-net amount`                     IS A NUMBER  -- s 8(1A); s 10A item 3
    `the concessional safety-net amount`        IS A NUMBER  -- s 8(1A); s 10A item 4
    `the FTB(A) safety-net amount`              IS A NUMBER  -- s 8(1A); s 10A item 5
    `the extended general safety-net amount`    IS A NUMBER  -- s 8(1A); s 10A item 6

`the safety-net amounts as printed in Compilation No. 136` MEANS `Safety-net amounts` WITH
    `the safety-net amount`                     IS 246
    `the concessional safety-net amount`        IS 500
    `the FTB(A) safety-net amount`              IS 500
    `the extended general safety-net amount`    IS 2000

@export What is my patient contribution for a service, in dollars (s 8(1A))?
GIVEN `the Schedule fee` IS A NUMBER @desc The Schedule fee for the item, in dollars
      `the medical expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc What you were charged for the service, in dollars
      `my ordinary benefit` IS A NUMBER @desc Your Medicare benefit apart from the safety nets, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my patient contribution` MEANS
    `the greater of` 0 (`the lesser of` `the Schedule fee` `the medical expenses` MINUS `my ordinary benefit`)

@export Is my service a relevant service for the Medicare safety nets (ss 10AC(1), 10ACA(1))?
GIVEN `a benefit is payable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a Medicare benefit is payable for the service
      `the medical expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc What you were charged for the service, in dollars
      `my ordinary benefit` IS A NUMBER @desc Your Medicare benefit apart from the safety nets, in dollars
      `given while I was receiving hospital treatment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were receiving hospital treatment (or hospital-substitute treatment with a private insurer benefit) at the time
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my service a relevant service` IF
        `a benefit is payable`
    AND `the medical expenses` GREATER THAN `my ordinary benefit`
    AND (NOT `given while I was receiving hospital treatment`)

@export Has my family or I reached the Medicare safety net this year with this claim (ss 10AC(2), 10AD(3))?
GIVEN `the amounts` IS A `Safety-net amounts` @desc The safety-net amounts in force for the year (indexed)
      `relevant service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this service is a relevant service
      `the bills have been paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the medical expenses for this and the earlier services have been paid
      `patient contributions already paid this year` IS A NUMBER @desc The total patient contributions paid on your (or your registered family's) earlier claims this year, in dollars
      `patient contribution for this claim` IS A NUMBER @desc The patient contribution for this claim, in dollars
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I reached the Medicare safety net` IF
        `relevant service`
    AND `the bills have been paid`
    AND `patient contributions already paid this year` PLUS `patient contribution for this claim`
            AT LEAST `the amounts`'s `the safety-net amount`

@export Is this the claim that takes me over the Medicare safety net (the threshold claim, ss 10AC(2), 10AD(3))?
GIVEN `the amounts` IS A `Safety-net amounts` @desc The safety-net amounts in force for the year (indexed)
      `relevant service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this service is a relevant service
      `the bills have been paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the medical expenses have been paid
      `patient contributions already paid this year` IS A NUMBER @desc The total patient contributions paid on earlier claims this year, in dollars
      `patient contribution for this claim` IS A NUMBER @desc The patient contribution for this claim, in dollars
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this my threshold claim` IF
        `Have I reached the Medicare safety net` `the amounts` `relevant service` `the bills have been paid`
            `patient contributions already paid this year` `patient contribution for this claim`
    AND `patient contributions already paid this year` LESS THAN `the amounts`'s `the safety-net amount`

@export By how much does the Medicare safety net increase my benefit, in dollars (ss 10AC(2), 10AD(3))?
GIVEN `the amounts` IS A `Safety-net amounts` @desc The safety-net amounts in force for the year (indexed)
      `relevant service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this service is a relevant service
      `the bills have been paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the medical expenses have been paid
      `patient contributions already paid this year` IS A NUMBER @desc The total patient contributions paid on earlier claims this year, in dollars
      `patient contribution for this claim` IS A NUMBER @desc The patient contribution for this claim, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`By how much does the Medicare safety net increase my benefit` MEANS
    IF `Have I reached the Medicare safety net` `the amounts` `relevant service` `the bills have been paid`
           `patient contributions already paid this year` `patient contribution for this claim`
    THEN `patient contribution for this claim`
    ELSE 0

§§ `ss 8(1A), 10ACA, 10ADA -- the extended Medicare safety net`

-- s 10ADA(3) (s 10ACA(2) for a registered family): "the benefit payable in respect of the claim is increased by 80% of the
-- out-of-pocket expenses for the current claim". (4): "The out-of-pocket expenses for a claim are: (a) the medical expenses
-- incurred in respect of a relevant service ...; reduced by: (b) any amounts payable under any other section of this Act in
-- respect of those expenses." (5): it applies if the claim is for a relevant service rendered to the person; "(c) the person has
-- paid at least 20% of the out-of-pocket expenses for the service directly to the person by whom, or on whose behalf, the service
-- was rendered"; the claim is accepted; and "(e) ... (i) the person is a concessional person ... and the concessional safety-net
-- applies ...; (ii) the extended general safety-net applies". s 10ACA(4)(e)(ii) adds, for a family, "a member of an FTB(A)
-- family ... and the FTB(A) safety-net applies". (6): a safety-net applies if "the sum of the out-of-pocket expenses for the
-- current claim and all relevant prior claims ... is equal to or exceeds the applicable safety-net amount".
-- (8): if the prior claims alone are below the amount, the benefit "is not increased under subsection (3) but is instead increased
-- by the amount worked out using the formula:" -- and the formula is missing from the deposit (an image lost in conversion, an
-- inference). That straddling increase is an INPUT.
-- s 8(1A): "concessional person": after the first time in the year the person is a concessional beneficiary under Part VII of
-- the National Health Act 1953 (asked as a fact). "FTB(A) family": a registered family after a member is first paid an
-- instalment of family tax benefit with a Part A rate above nil (asked as a fact). Amounts: concessional $500, FTB(A) $500,
-- extended general $2,000 (indexed).
-- ENCODING CHOICE: where more than one safety-net could apply, the lowest applicable amount is the one tested (the Act asks only
-- that "one or more" apply). The concessional safety-net counts only concessional members' claims (s 10ACA(6)(a)(i)); the
-- patient states the prior out-of-pocket expenses that count for it.
DECLARE `My extended safety-net claim` HAS
    `it is for a relevant service`                                           IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 10ADA(5)(a)
    `out-of-pocket expenses for this claim`                                  IS A NUMBER   -- s 10ADA(4)
    `out-of-pocket expenses on earlier claims this year`                     IS A NUMBER   -- s 10ADA(6), (7)
    `I paid at least 20% of the out-of-pocket expenses directly to the professional` IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 10ADA(5)(c)
    `I am a concessional person this year`                                   IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 10ADA(5)(e)(i)
    `my registered family is an FTB(A) family this year`                     IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 10ACA(4)(e)(ii)

@export What are my out-of-pocket expenses for the extended safety net, in dollars (s 10ADA(4))?
GIVEN `the medical expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc What you were charged for the service, in dollars
      `benefits payable under other sections` IS A NUMBER @desc Your Medicare benefit for the service, including any increase under the original safety net, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What are my out-of-pocket expenses for the extended safety net` MEANS
    `the greater of` 0 (`the medical expenses` MINUS `benefits payable under other sections`)

@export Which extended safety-net amount applies to me, in dollars (ss 8(1A), 10ACA(4)(e), 10ADA(5)(e))?
GIVEN `the amounts` IS A `Safety-net amounts` @desc The safety-net amounts in force for the year (indexed)
      `the claim` IS A `My extended safety-net claim` @desc Your claim and whether you are a concessional person or an FTB(A) family
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Which extended safety-net amount applies to me` MEANS
    IF `the claim`'s `I am a concessional person this year`
    THEN `the lesser of` (`the amounts`'s `the concessional safety-net amount`) `the FTB(A) or general amount`
    ELSE `the FTB(A) or general amount`
    WHERE
        `the FTB(A) or general amount` MEANS
            IF `the claim`'s `my registered family is an FTB(A) family this year`
            THEN `the lesser of` (`the amounts`'s `the FTB(A) safety-net amount`) (`the amounts`'s `the extended general safety-net amount`)
            ELSE `the amounts`'s `the extended general safety-net amount`

@export Does the extended Medicare safety net apply to my claim (ss 10ACA(4), (5), 10ADA(5), (6))?
GIVEN `the amounts` IS A `Safety-net amounts` @desc The safety-net amounts in force for the year (indexed)
      `the claim` IS A `My extended safety-net claim` @desc Your claim, what you paid, and your out-of-pocket expenses this year
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the extended safety net apply to my claim` IF
        `the claim`'s `it is for a relevant service`
    AND `the claim`'s `I paid at least 20% of the out-of-pocket expenses directly to the professional`
    AND `the claim`'s `out-of-pocket expenses for this claim` PLUS `the claim`'s `out-of-pocket expenses on earlier claims this year`
            AT LEAST `Which extended safety-net amount applies to me` `the amounts` `the claim`

@export By how much does the extended Medicare safety net increase my benefit, in dollars (ss 10ACA(2), (7), 10ADA(3), (8))?
GIVEN `the amounts` IS A `Safety-net amounts` @desc The safety-net amounts in force for the year (indexed)
      `the claim` IS A `My extended safety-net claim` @desc Your claim, what you paid, and your out-of-pocket expenses this year
      `the s 10ADA(8) formula amount` IS A NUMBER @desc For the claim that crosses the threshold only: the increase worked out by the formula in s 10ADA(8) (or s 10ACA(7)), which is missing from the deposited text
GIVETH A NUMBER
`By how much does the extended safety net increase my benefit` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`Does the extended safety net apply to my claim` `the amounts` `the claim`))
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF `the claim`'s `out-of-pocket expenses on earlier claims this year`
                AT LEAST `Which extended safety-net amount applies to me` `the amounts` `the claim`
         THEN `the claim`'s `out-of-pocket expenses for this claim` TIMES 80 DIVIDED BY 100
         ELSE `the s 10ADA(8) formula amount`

§§ `ss 3(1), 128C; Regulations s 90 -- can I be charged as a public patient in a public hospital`

-- s 3(1): "public hospital service means a hospital service provided in: (a) a recognised hospital; or (b) a hospital in respect
-- of which the Commonwealth, or a State, provides funding for the provision of hospital services to public patients." "public
-- patient, in relation to a hospital, means a patient in respect of whom the hospital provides comprehensive care, including all
-- necessary medical, nursing and diagnostic services ...". "recognised hospital" is one with a statement under s 121-5(8) of the
-- Private Health Insurance Act 2007 that it is a public hospital (asked as a fact).
-- s 128C(1): "A person mentioned in subsection (2) must not, in circumstances set out in the regulations: (a) charge a fee for the
-- provision of a public hospital service; or (b) receive any payment or other consideration from anyone in respect of the
-- provision of a public hospital service; if the person knows that the person to whom the service is ... provided is, or intends
-- to be, a public patient in the hospital. Penalty: 50 penalty units." (2): "(a) a medical practitioner; (b) a participating
-- midwife; (c) a participating nurse practitioner; (d) a person acting on behalf of" one of them.
-- Regulations s 90: "the circumstances in which a fee must not be charged ... for the provision of a public hospital service are
-- that the service is: (a) for attendance at, or associated with, the delivery of a baby; or (b) requested or required by the
-- person to whom the service is provided in connection with the delivery of a baby."
-- So the bar reaches only childbirth, and the hospital itself is not in the s 128C(2) list. Medicare benefits do not reach
-- public-hospital charges either (s 17(1)(a); s 19(2)). Whatever else protects a public patient from charges is not in this Act.
DECLARE `Who is charging me` IS ONE OF
    `a medical practitioner`
    `a participating midwife`
    `a participating nurse practitioner`
    `a person acting for a practitioner, midwife or nurse practitioner`
    `the hospital itself`

@export Is my hospital care a public hospital service (s 3(1))?
GIVEN `in a recognised hospital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the hospital is a recognised (public) hospital
      `in a hospital publicly funded for public patients` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commonwealth or a State funds the hospital to treat public patients
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my care a public hospital service` IF
    `in a recognised hospital` OR `in a hospital publicly funded for public patients`

@export Does s 128C forbid charging me for my care as a public patient (s 128C; Regulations s 90)?
GIVEN `who` IS A `Who is charging me` @desc Who wants to charge you
      `in a recognised hospital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the hospital is a recognised (public) hospital
      `in a hospital publicly funded for public patients` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commonwealth or a State funds the hospital to treat public patients
      `they know I am or intend to be a public patient` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person charging knows you are, or intend to be, a public patient
      `the service is connected with the delivery of a baby` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the service is attendance at or associated with the birth of a baby, or requested in connection with it (Regulations s 90)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does s 128C forbid charging me` IF
        `Is my care a public hospital service` `in a recognised hospital` `in a hospital publicly funded for public patients`
    AND `they know I am or intend to be a public patient`
    AND `the service is connected with the delivery of a baby`
    AND CONSIDER `who`
        WHEN `the hospital itself` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

@export What is the most a practitioner can be fined for charging me as a public patient, in penalty units (s 128C(1))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most a practitioner can be fined for charging me` MEANS 50
